#!/usr/bin/env python3
from pathlib import Path
Path('/app/answer.json').write_text('{"answer": "The type-safe dictionary structure (TypedDict) used as a view function return type annotation decouples JSON response serialization from HTTP status representation through Flask\'s type system and runtime handling.\\n\\n**Type System Design:**\\nIn `src/flask/typing.py`, the `ResponseValue` type union includes `t.Mapping[str, t.Any]` with a comment noting \\"Only dict is actually accepted, but Mapping allows for TypedDict\\" (line 17-18). This allows type checkers to validate TypedDict structures while Flask\'s runtime accepts them as regular dictionaries.\\n\\n**Runtime Handling:**\\nWhen a view function returns a TypedDict instance (like `StatusJSON` from `tests/type_check/typing_route.py`), Flask\'s `make_response` method in `src/flask/app.py` treats it as a regular dict at runtime. At line 1230, the code checks `isinstance(rv, (dict, list))` and converts it to JSON using `self.json.response(rv)` (line 1231), which serializes the dictionary structure to a JSON response.\\n\\n**Separation of Concerns:**\\nHTTP status codes are handled separately from the JSON payload structure:\\n- Status codes can be specified via tuple returns: `(dict, status_code)` or `(dict, status_code, headers)` (lines 1155-1162 in `app.py`)\\n- The status code is set on the Response object separately after JSON serialization (lines 1259-1263)\\n- The TypedDict defines only the JSON payload structure, not HTTP metadata\\n\\n**Type Safety Across Boundaries:**\\nThis maintains type safety because:\\n1. Type checkers validate the TypedDict structure at development time\\n2. Flask\'s runtime doesn\'t need special TypedDict handling\\u2014it processes them as dicts\\n3. HTTP status representation (status codes, headers) is handled by Flask\'s framework separately from the JSON data structure\\n4. The separation allows type checkers to validate JSON payload structure independently of HTTP concerns\\n\\nThis pattern was introduced in Flask 2.1.3 (as noted in `CHANGES.rst` line 338-339: \\"When type checking, allow TypedDict to be returned from view functions\\"), enabling type-safe JSON responses while maintaining framework flexibility for HTTP status handling."}' + '\n')
